WEBVTT

00:00:00.430 --> 00:00:06.310
In the name of the Father and of the Son and of the Holy Spirit, Amen.

00:00:06.310 --> 00:00:13.390
The reading from the Sinaxadion for October 3rd, on which we commemorate the Holy

00:00:13.390 --> 00:00:19.340
Hyromarter, Dionysius, the Ariopagite.

00:00:19.340 --> 00:00:25.560
On the 3rd of the month we celebrate the memory of the Holy Hyromarter, Dionysius, the

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:28.380
Ariopagite.

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:37.660
And Dionysius, who came of a rich and noble family, lived in Athens at the time of the apostles.

00:00:37.660 --> 00:00:43.540
On account of the wisdom and virtue pagan learning afforded him, he was chosen one of the

00:00:43.540 --> 00:00:51.060
nine counselors of the Ariopagus, the High Court and Parliament of the city.

00:00:51.060 --> 00:00:57.580
As such it was he who invited the great apostle Paul, whom the Holy Spirit had brought to

00:00:57.580 --> 00:01:03.860
the city to proclaim the good tidings of salvation on the Ariopagus.

00:01:03.860 --> 00:01:10.020
From the height of this rock, overlooking the city, the simple tentmaker pulled to pieces

00:01:10.020 --> 00:01:16.860
the sophistries of the Athenian philosophers and clearly showed that the unknown God,

00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:23.620
whom their unassisted reason had given them a vague notion of, was the Lord of heaven

00:01:23.620 --> 00:01:30.540
and earth, who made the world and everything in it, and who does not live in temples made

00:01:30.540 --> 00:01:39.940
by hands, as though he needed anything, since he himself gives to all men life and breath

00:01:39.940 --> 00:01:42.900
and everything.

00:01:42.900 --> 00:01:49.700
He told them that man is made in the image of God and is called upon to share the divine

00:01:49.700 --> 00:01:56.820
life in the very Son of God, Jesus Christ, who has taken our flesh, has risen from the

00:01:56.820 --> 00:02:01.180
dead and will come to judge the world.

00:02:01.180 --> 00:02:08.300
Most of the audience mocked St. Paul, unhearing about the resurrection of the dead, since

00:02:08.300 --> 00:02:14.180
the false wisdom of this world had completely darkened their minds.

00:02:14.180 --> 00:02:21.740
And so the hearts of several among them, including St. Dionysius and St. Yetothil's, were

00:02:21.740 --> 00:02:28.340
touched by these words of eternal life, and they believed.

00:02:28.340 --> 00:02:36.220
When St. Paul spoke of the Savior's passion and of the portance that occurred at his death,

00:02:36.220 --> 00:02:43.660
Dionysius recalled the solar eclipse, inexplicable to astronomers that had happened years before

00:02:43.740 --> 00:02:50.780
when he was in Egypt, completing his studies among learned men at Heliopolis.

00:02:50.780 --> 00:02:58.980
Either God is suffering, he had cried out then, or this is the end of the world.

00:02:58.980 --> 00:03:05.140
This event prepared Dionysius and his master Yetothil's to recognize him who overcomes the

00:03:05.140 --> 00:03:12.460
laws of nature when he saw wills, so they listened eagerly to the holy apostles' teaching

00:03:12.460 --> 00:03:16.100
and asked him for baptism.

00:03:16.100 --> 00:03:22.940
After some time St. Paul departed to endure new tribulations and lift St. Yetothil's as

00:03:22.940 --> 00:03:25.460
Bishop of Athens.

00:03:25.460 --> 00:03:30.900
Like the eagle that can look directly upon the brightness of the sun, Yetothil's was able

00:03:30.900 --> 00:03:37.700
to enter into the mysteries of God, but he wrote little, choosing rather to instruct his

00:03:37.780 --> 00:03:45.820
disciple Dionysius, orally, concerning the revelations beyond all speech that God granted

00:03:45.820 --> 00:03:47.620
him.

00:03:47.620 --> 00:03:54.340
On Yetothil's death Dionysius became Bishop of Athens in his stead.

00:03:54.340 --> 00:04:00.820
God enabled him by his grace to put into writing the sublime teachings of his master about

00:04:00.820 --> 00:04:06.740
the unutterable boundlessness of the divine nature, to which none but the negative terms

00:04:06.740 --> 00:04:14.340
of apophatic theology are applicable, and about the unfathomable riches of his revelation

00:04:14.340 --> 00:04:21.940
through his names and energies, that is the sum of affirmative theology.

00:04:21.940 --> 00:04:31.340
He described how the sensible world that perceived by our senses and the intelligible world that

00:04:31.340 --> 00:04:38.780
apprehended by the illumined intellect are united to God in a magnificently ordered hierarchy.

00:04:38.780 --> 00:04:45.220
He explained how the ecclesiastical hierarchy, from the bishop to the monk, manifests upon

00:04:45.220 --> 00:04:52.700
the earth the nine orders of angels, and how the divine light is distributed to each person

00:04:52.700 --> 00:04:57.100
according to his degree of purification.

00:04:57.100 --> 00:05:02.500
Though some people have accused Saint Dionysius of borrowing the terminology of the neoplatonic

00:05:02.500 --> 00:05:09.900
philosophers, the Orthodox Church, enlightened by his divine teachings, believes rather that

00:05:09.900 --> 00:05:16.580
it is the latter who have borrowed his language, albeit without being able to show, as does

00:05:16.580 --> 00:05:23.580
the saint, that he who is beyond every name and all being, and who dwells in the darkness

00:05:23.580 --> 00:05:33.340
more radiant than light, has appeared in the flesh so as to make us partakers of his light.

00:05:33.340 --> 00:05:39.660
Saint Dionysius attended such heights of divine contemplation that he was accounted worthy

00:05:39.660 --> 00:05:46.180
of being numbered among the apostles, and was wondrously transported to Jerusalem for the

00:05:46.180 --> 00:05:50.100
entombment of the mother of God.

00:05:50.100 --> 00:05:56.580
On his return to Athens, he devoted himself for some time to converting the pagans and

00:05:56.580 --> 00:05:59.980
to guiding his spiritual flock.

00:05:59.980 --> 00:06:06.420
Towards the end of Nero's reign, he visited Rome to give his master Saint Paul an account

00:06:06.420 --> 00:06:09.300
of his missionary activity.

00:06:09.300 --> 00:06:15.340
He was present at Paul's martyrdom and then returned to Greece.

00:06:15.340 --> 00:06:21.860
On a later visit to Rome, Saint Dionysius and his disciples, the priest Rousticus and

00:06:21.860 --> 00:06:28.060
the Deacon Elifetios, were commissioned by Saint Clement, the bishop of Rome, to preach

00:06:28.060 --> 00:06:31.060
the gospel in Gaul.

00:06:31.060 --> 00:06:38.820
When he had preached the word of truth in a good many places, Dionysius settled in Paris,

00:06:38.820 --> 00:06:45.420
which was then a small town sunk in the darkness of ignorance and paganism.

00:06:45.420 --> 00:06:51.420
He built a church there in which he served the Holy Mysteries and proclaimed the great works

00:06:51.420 --> 00:06:53.060
of God.

00:06:53.060 --> 00:06:59.340
He worked many miracles so that in a while the number of his disciples increased and they

00:06:59.340 --> 00:07:06.060
set out to spread the Holy Gospel in Britain as far as Spain.

00:07:06.060 --> 00:07:12.180
The renown of Saint Dionysius aroused the envy of the devil, who gave the emperor

00:07:12.180 --> 00:07:18.540
demission to understand that the Greek bishop, who was preaching a new God, was trying

00:07:18.540 --> 00:07:22.940
to provoke disorder and revolt.

00:07:22.940 --> 00:07:30.060
The imperial officers tried in vain to persuade Dionysius and his companions to deny God, for

00:07:30.140 --> 00:07:37.540
whom they lived and wished to die, and so on being sentenced to beheading the martyrs

00:07:37.540 --> 00:07:40.060
were overjoyed.

00:07:40.060 --> 00:07:45.740
Not only did God give the Holy Bishop the grace of knowledge and of teaching, but he also

00:07:45.740 --> 00:07:53.420
wanted to show in his martyrdom that by faith Christians have overcome death.

00:07:53.420 --> 00:08:02.260
So when Dionysius had been beheaded, he stood up to the amazement of all, took his head

00:08:02.260 --> 00:08:11.100
in his hands, and walked thus for two miles until he met Cattula, a godly woman, to whom

00:08:11.100 --> 00:08:14.380
he gave this precious relic.

00:08:14.380 --> 00:08:22.860
Saint Dionysius' skull is now venerated in the monastery of Dochiadio on Mount Athos, to which

00:08:22.860 --> 00:08:31.510
it was given by the emperor Alexius Comnenus in the 11th century.

00:08:31.510 --> 00:08:38.790
Through the prayers of our Holy Father's, O Lord Jesus Christ our God, have mercy on us,

00:08:38.790 --> 00:08:39.790
and save us.
